l/117781","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117781.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117781.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"This is a \"simplification\" of #107226 that moves the silence frames logic back into AudioServer. It also introduces the play_scheduled_relative method that allows sounds to be played relative to another playback.\r\n\r\nWhile fixing audio mixing performance, game performance still suffers due to AudioServer methods taking O(N) time to run. Additionally, I tried adding `play_scheduled_relative` method, but this doesn't work well when the base playback is paused or if played from not the beginning of the clip. Having a true `play_scheduled_relative` method would need relative silence frames rather than absolute ones.\r\n\r\nDemo project: [MetronomeAbsolute.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/26292054/MetronomeAbsolute.zip)\r\n\r\nTODOs:\r\n* ScheduledAudioStreamPlayer2D/3D counterparts\r\n* Fix game frame performance with many scheduled sounds\r\n* Address issues with `play_scheduled_relative`\r\n\r\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117781/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117781/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}